447 - Long Upon the Mountains
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 447
Topic: Early Advent - 

Verse 1:
[F]Long upon the [C]mountains [F]weary,
Have the scattered [C7]flocks been [F]torn;
Dark the dessert [C]paths, and [F]dreary;
Grievous trials [C7]have they [F]borne.
[F]Now the gathering [Bb]call is [F]sounding,
Solemn in its [Bb]warning [F]voice;
Union, faith, and [C]love, a[F]bounding,
Bid the little [C7]flock re[F]joice.

Verse 2:
[F]Now the [C]light of [F]truth they're seeking,
[C7]In its [F]onward track pursue;
[C]All the [F]ten commandments keeping,
[C7]They are holy, [F]just, and true.
[F]On the [Bb]words of [F]lire they're feeding,
[Bb]Precious to their [F]taste so sweet;
[C]All their [F]Master's percepts heeding,
[C7]Bowing humbly [F]to His feet.

Verse 3:
[F]In that [C]light of [F]light and beauty,
[C7]In that [F]golden city fair,
[C]Soon its pearly [F]gates they'll enter,
[C7]And of all [F]its glories share.
[F]There, [Bb]divine the [F]soul's expansions;
[Bb]Free from sin, [F]and death, and pain;
[C]Tear will never [F]dim those mansions
[C7]Where the [F]souls immortal reign.

Verse 4:
[F]Soon He [C]comes! With [F]clouds descending;
[C7]All His [F]saints, entombed arise;
[C]The redeemed, [F]in anthems blending,
[C7]Shout their vict'ry [F]thro' the skies.
[F]O, we [Bb]long for [F]Thine appearing;
[Bb]Come, O [F]Savior, quickly come!
[C]Blessed hope! [F]Our spirits cheering,
[C7]Take thy [F]ransomed children home.
